Check A: how large are NIC drops on Claims hosts, as a rate and as a share of packets?

timeseries {drx = avg(dt.host.net.nic.packets.dropped_rx),
            dtx = avg(dt.host.net.nic.packets.dropped_tx),
            prx = avg(dt.host.net.nic.packets.rx),
            ptx = avg(dt.host.net.nic.packets.tx)},
           by:{dt.entity.host, dt.entity.network_interface}, from:-2h
| fieldsAdd dropRate = coalesce(arrayAvg(drx), 0) + coalesce(arrayAvg(dtx), 0),
            pktRate  = coalesce(arrayAvg(prx), 0) + coalesce(arrayAvg(ptx), 0)
| fieldsAdd dropPct = if(pktRate > 0, 100.0 * dropRate / pktRate, else: 0.0)
| lookup [ fetch dt.entity.host | fields id, tags ],
         sourceField: dt.entity.host, lookupField: id, prefix: "e."
| expand tag = e.tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| summarize interfaces      = countDistinctExact(dt.entity.network_interface),
            withDrops       = countDistinctExact(if(dropRate > 0, dt.entity.network_interface)),
            `drops >= 0.1%` = countDistinctExact(if(dropPct >= 0.1, dt.entity.network_interface)),
            `drops >= 1%`   = countDistinctExact(if(dropPct >= 1, dt.entity.network_interface)),
            `drops >= 5%`   = countDistinctExact(if(dropPct >= 5, dt.entity.network_interface)),
            maxDropRate     = round(max(dropRate), decimals:2),
            maxDropPct      = round(max(dropPct), decimals:2)


This returns one row. It shows where a drop threshold would sit, so we don't flag 52 hosts for a handful of dropped packets. I haven't confirmed that packets.rx and packets.tx carry the interface dimension. If it errors, tell me.

Check B: retransmissions as a percentage of packets sent, per app

timeseries {re = avg(dt.process.network.packets.re_tx_aggr),
            tx = avg(dt.process.network.packets.tx)},
           by:{dt.entity.process_group_instance}, from:-2h
| fieldsAdd reRate = coalesce(arrayAvg(re), 0),
            txRate = coalesce(arrayAvg(tx), 0)
| lookup [ fetch dt.entity.process_group_instance | fields id, tags ],
         sourceField: dt.entity.process_group_instance, lookupField: id, prefix: "e."
| expand tag = e.tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| summarize processes = countDistinctExact(dt.entity.process_group_instance),
            reRate    = round(sum(reRate), decimals:2),
            txRate    = round(sum(txRate), decimals:0),
            by:{apmid}
| fieldsAdd retransPct = if(txRate > 0, round(100.0 * reRate / txRate, decimals:2), else: 0.0)
| sort retransPct desc


This assumes packets.tx is the right total to divide by. I haven't confirmed that. Please open dt.process.network.packets.base_re_tx_aggr in the metric browser and send me its Description, because it may be the intended base for a retransmission ratio. If a few apps have a very high percentage on very low traffic, I'll add a minimum-traffic filter.

Optional: resets and timeouts using the _local variants

timeseries {rs = avg(dt.process.network.sessions.reset_local),
            to = avg(dt.process.network.sessions.timeout_local)},
           by:{dt.entity.process_group_instance}, from:-2h
| fieldsAdd rs = coalesce(arrayAvg(rs), 0), to = coalesce(arrayAvg(to), 0)
| lookup [ fetch dt.entity.process_group_instance | fields id, tags ],
         sourceField: dt.entity.process_group_instance, lookupField: id, prefix: "e."
| expand tag = e.tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| summarize processes = countDistinctExact(dt.entity.process_group_instance),
            resets = round(sum(rs), decimals:2), timeouts = round(sum(to), decimals:2),
            by:{apmid}
| filter resets > 0 or timeouts > 0
| sort resets desc
